# Triton and torch.inductor JIT-compile vLLM's kernels at run time, and need a
# full build toolchain for the launcher stubs they emit; without it the engine
# core dies before it registers and the pod answers 502.
#
# Found one layer at a time, each on a real olmOCR pod:
#   gcc          — the C compiler
#   g++          — the launcher Triton builds is C++, so gcc alone is not enough
#   ninja-build  — inductor shells out to ninja to build its extensions
# libc6-dev is the headers both compilers need.
#
# Kept (not purged) because the compilation happens at RUN time on the pod, not
# at build time.
gcc
g++
ninja-build
libc6-dev
